ifa/158 -- every type violation is now fatal (2026-09-17), and this program has real ones: `a.x` is reassigned across a bound method, a 1-arg lambda and another class's method, so `a.x(2)` cannot be typed. pyc reports `illegal call argument type expression illegal: int64 / closure` at the call. It previously compiled with those as WARNINGS and ran, which is exactly what ifa/158 refuses -- emitting a binary whose analysis did not type. The check file records the old passing output, so this flips to PASS when the dispatch is resolved (a per-assignment split of the attribute, not boxing).
